        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: preserve prompt cache prefixes across room-event runs",
        "body": "Related: #102175\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nLong-lived group-channel sessions can lose prompt-cache reuse when an ambient\n`room_event` changes cache-visible delivery instructions or owner-only tool\nschemas, even though the session and model are unchanged.\n\nThis PR stabilizes the prompt/tool shape for that room-event path while keeping\nactual delivery and authorization strict.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Separates effective source delivery from the prompt-facing delivery mode.\n  Ambient room events can still require `message_tool_only` delivery without\n  rewriting the session's cache-visible reply contract.\n- Threads the prompt-facing mode through primary runs, queued followups,\n  embedded/context-engine runs, and the Codex app-server prompt/tool builders.\n- Gives owner and non-owner ambient room events the same safe owner-only core\n  tool inventory. Direct owner turns still receive `cron`, `gateway`, and\n  `nodes`; explicit non-owner execution remains blocked.\n- Keeps effective delivery responsible for forcing the `message` tool, so this\n  does not relax visible-reply routing.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRedacted same-session traces from the reporter's Discord room-event flow showed:\n\n- tool inventory flipping between `44` and `47` tools when sender policy changed;\n- cache reads falling to roughly `2k-10k`, then repeatedly ceilinging around\n  `37k-40k`, despite an otherwise warm long-lived session;\n- after the room-event prompt/tool fixes, warm turns with stable inventory\n  reached roughly `49k-52k` cached tokens on approximately `51k-55k` context.\n\nThese numbers establish the room-event invalidator and its local improvement;\nthey do not claim to solve every provider-side cache miss.\n\n## Validation\n\nCurrent head: `8038ca2a2ec5bde1540dced55b789d1cc9d0de64`, rebased onto upstream `main`\n`1d4c17073cbef6b4c20df029b4dcbdbcf5ba99ca` at validation time.\n\n- Focused regression suite: **9 files, 704 tests passed**.\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Commit hooks/formatter passed on all 20 changed files.\n\n## Known Gap\n\nThis remains a draft because prompt-facing delivery mode is not yet threaded\nthrough every compaction entry point. In-attempt context-engine compaction keeps\nit, but preflight/manual/queued-direct compaction can rebuild prompt/tool state\nwithout the stable mode. That follow-up needs a focused regression test before\nthis is ready.\n\n## Explicitly Out of Scope\n\nThis PR does **not** claim to fix native GPT-5.5 ChatGPT/Codex Responses cache\ncontinuation. An earlier version tried moving the dynamic prompt suffix into a\npost-history developer item; the native backend rejected that payload with HTTP\n400. Those Responses changes were removed from this rebuild and need a separate\ntransport-level investigation.\n\nDisclaimer: This PR was filed and updated autonomously by Codex on behalf of the\nreporter. Private user, channel, host, credential, and full trace identifiers\nwere removed from the evidence.",
        "branch": "codex/stabilize-room-event-prompt-cache",
